Q: How to print page without print preview from Stimulsoft in Web Api A: <p><code>mainReport.Print(false)</code> in a Web API will try to print from the <strong>server machine</strong>, not the user's browser/PC. So when you hit:</p>
<pre><code>http://localhost:9090/api/printPage
</code></pre>
<p>the backend sends a print job from ASP.NET, not the client browser. This is usually not ideal because:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The API runs under IIS/service credentials, not the logged-in user.</p>
</li>
<li><p>The server may not have a default printer configured.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Web apps shouldn't trigger print dialogs on the server.</p>
</li>
<li><p>A browser can't be forced to print from a server-side request.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The recommended approach is to generate a PDF in the API and let the browser handle printing. Example:</p>
<pre><code>[HttpGet]
[Route(&quot;PrintPage&quot;)]
public HttpResponseMessage PrintPage()
{
    var persons = new List&lt;Person&gt;
    {
        new Person { Id = 1, FirstName = &quot;omid&quot;, LastName = &quot;nasri&quot;, Gender = true },
        new Person { Id = 2, FirstName = &quot;hana&quot;, LastName = &quot;akbari&quot;, Gender = false },
        new Person { Id = 3, FirstName = &quot;ali&quot;, LastName = &quot;jahani&quot;, Gender = true },
        new Person { Id = 4, FirstName = &quot;sara&quot;, LastName = &quot;sabori&quot;, Gender = false }
    };

    var report = new StiReport();
    report.Load(@&quot;D:\WebSite\Web\Print\Report.mrt&quot;);
    report.RegBusinessObject(&quot;persons&quot;, persons);
    report.Render();

    var stream = new MemoryStream();
    report.ExportDocument(StiExportFormat.Pdf, stream);
    stream.Position = 0;

    var response = new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK);
    response.Content = new StreamContent(stream);
    response.Content.Headers.ContentType =
        new System.Net.Http.Headers.MediaTypeHeaderValue(&quot;application/pdf&quot;);

    response.Content.Headers.ContentDisposition =
        new System.Net.Http.Headers.ContentDispositionHeaderValue(&quot;inline&quot;)
        {
            FileName = &quot;Report.pdf&quot;
        };

    return response;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then open it from the frontend:</p>
<pre><code>window.open('/api/printPage', '_blank');
</code></pre>
